REPRODUCER-ONLY PATCH -- not a fix.

This is applied at build time to a build-local checkout of oneTBB
(https://github.com/uxlfoundation/oneTBB, tag v2023.1.0).  It is *not*
intended for upstream.  It parks the main thread inside libtcm's
exit-time destructor so that the dlclose() performed by a oneTBB worker
thread is guaranteed to land in the vulnerable window.

Root cause: at process exit a oneTBB worker runs

    governor::release_resources() -> dynamic_unlink_all()
        -> dlclose(libtcm.so.1)

while the main thread is executing libtcm's __cxa_atexit destructor
(hwloc_topology_loader_t::~hwloc_topology_loader_t).  glibc 2.43 protects
DSO destructors that run from _dl_fini() by bumping l_direct_opencount,
but that protection is absent when the destructor is dispatched from
__run_exit_handlers() (which is what happens when libtcm was dlopen()ed
after _dl_fini was registered -- i.e. when oneTBB itself is loaded from a
dlopen()ed Python extension rather than as a startup DT_NEEDED).  The
worker's dlclose() then unmaps libtcm out from under the main thread.

diff --git a/thread_composability_manager/include/tcm/detail/hwloc_utils.h b/thread_composability_manager/include/tcm/detail/hwloc_utils.h
index d16b8e4..7811366 100644
--- a/thread_composability_manager/include/tcm/detail/hwloc_utils.h
+++ b/thread_composability_manager/include/tcm/detail/hwloc_utils.h
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #ifndef __TCM_HWLOC_UTILS_HEADER
 #define __TCM_HWLOC_UTILS_HEADER
 
+#include <chrono>
 #include <vector>
 #include <thread>               // std::this_thread::yield()
 
@@ -75,6 +76,11 @@ public:
         if (is_initialized) {
             while (spin_mutex.test_and_set()) { std::this_thread::yield(); }
             hwloc_topology_destroy(topology);
+            // REPRODUCER PATCH: widen the race window.  While the main thread
+            // is parked here, inside libtcm code, a oneTBB worker thread can run
+            // governor::release_resources() -> dynamic_unlink_all() -> dlclose(libtcm)
+            // and unmap libtcm.  The write to is_initialized below then faults.
+            std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(1000));
             is_initialized = false;
             spin_mutex.clear();
         }
